  "id": "exelon",
  "term": "Exelon",
  "definition": "Exelon is the tartrate salt form of rivastigmine, a drug described as having cognitive-stimulating effects. It may work by reversibly binding to cholinesterase, which reduces the breakdown of acetylcholine and increases cholinergic activity.",
